      "bullets": [
        "Modern OpenSSH private keys use the native `openssh-key-v1` format with bcrypt KDF key derivation to resist offline brute-force attacks.",
        "Key files feature magic header bytes followed by packed binary wire formats encoding cipher settings, public parameters, and encrypted private blocks.",
        "Parsing native OpenSSH key blobs requires handling length-prefixed byte arrays, salt/rounds metadata, and unpadded payload alignment for credential extraction."
      ]
